{"source":"user-event","type":"click","text":"C\n    \n      Hybrid: Canvas-Direct + Selective Layer Caching\n      Best balance of performance and simplicity\n      Starts with Approach A's Canvas-direct rendering as the foundation. Adds lightweight layer separation — grid/axes use drawWithCache (redraws only when axis config changes), data layer redraws per frame. No RenderNode complexity.\n\n      \n        How it handles WebSocket updates:\n        \n          Frame-batched data updates (same as A)\n          Grid/axes cached via drawWithCache — only rebuild when config changes\n          Data layer uses onDrawWithContent — redraws per frame\n          Path caching for line charts — reuse path when only appending points\n        \n      \n\n      \n        \n          Pros\n          \n            Clean Compose APIs throughout — no Android graphics escape hatches\n            Grid/axes don't redraw on data changes\n            Path caching reduces draw cost for append-only updates\n            Simple enough to implement and maintain\n            Easy to upgrade to B later if needed\n          \n        \n        \n          Cons\n          \n            Not as fast as B for extreme datasets (50K+)\n            Still redraws data layer fully (though with path reuse)\n          \n        \n      \n\n      \n        Performance profile:\n        60fps with 10K+ points. Cached static layers via Compose APIs. Path reuse on appends. Upgradeable to RenderNode if needed.","choice":"c","id":null,"timestamp":1773423502341}
